  "name": "Question 10",
  "problem": "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14037461/assets/6f80319af7f362c2a902853687670a9dab8e88778521147942dfb9a0d9872b75.png)\n\nThe graph of $y=f(t)$ is shown above. Which of the following could be $f(t),$ where $u$ denotes the unit step function?",
  "worked_solution": "The unit step function $u(t)$ is defined as\n\n$$\nu(t)={\\begin{aligned}1,\\,t\\ge 0, \\\\ 0,\\,t<0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe graph of $y=u(t)$ is shown below.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14037461/assets/4f7a1a32f5c639ec0a9433fc6d330e5ea9f8ed6fa1602441b54c9158bb69f63e.png)\n\nNotice that to transform the function $y=u(t)$ to the given function $y=f(t),$ we perform the following transformations:\n\n- First, we shift $y=u(t)$ by one unit to the right, giving $y=u(t-1).$\n\n- Then, we scale by a scale factor of $2$ parallel to the $y$-axis, giving $y=2u(t-1).$\n\nTherefore, we conclude that $f(t)=2u(t-1).$",
